meras, where he discovered the other individual was slightly above room temperature. <br /> <br /> Julian immediately began investigating the individual with no heat signature, a local Ancilla Brujah Anarch, and uncovered the truth behind the existence of vampires. Julian was ecstatic at his luck, and immediately pressed the Brujah to expose him, unless he spilled everything about vampires. <br /> <br /> This created a bit of an uproar locally, and a sort of &quot;bloodhunt&quot; was called on Julian for breaking the Masquerade. The Brujah Anarch wanted to Embrace him for being so bold, but was beaten to it by the local Tremere Primogen. <br /> <br /> The Brujah Anarch never forgave the Primogen, and sees toying with Julian as a fine way to return the slight. <br /> <br /> Julian for one, enjoys being Tremere, despite needing to disappear from the hacker community and give up his millions to the Clan (it was confiscated by the Clan to complete his disappearance). He relates much of Thaumaturgy to hacking, and has taken to his studies with vigor. Despite his anarchistic background, he enjoys being on the &quot;inside&quot; pissing out far more than the outside pissing in (with Clan Tremere being the &quot;inside&quot;). He does, however, feel under utilized. The Regent and Primogen (his Sire) treat him like a sort of technological Auspex, which he somewhat resents, given what he knows he's capable of, as one of the world's foremost hackers. He spends his nights accumulating favors among the local Kindred population by uncovering information the local Nosferatu would froth at the mouth to obtain, and trying to prove to his Sire that he's more than just an Undead IT gopher. <br /> <br /> His current plans are mainly centered around rebuilding his wealth by siphoning money from rivals of his Sire, trading favors for more Thaumaturgical knowledge, and irking that Brujah Anarch who wanted to Sire him, who returns the favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link"